{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794508214,"nonce":"CoCGzxbzY3IBrIyuk3mblQXW9M4=","title":"caribou run: a threaded wasm module cannot reserve its 512 MB heap","message":"Caribou's test `caribou-driver/tests/linked.rs::futures_settle_in_a_threaded_wasm_program` fails. The program is built for `wasm32-wasip1-threads` by `caribou build` and run by `caribou run`; it aborts at start with:\n\n    thread '\u003cunnamed\u003e' (1) panicked at std/src/gc.rs:3046:9:\n    could not reserve 536870912 bytes for the heap\n\nEstablished:\n- It fails the same way with ash at d6128244 (LLVM built the module) and with ash at 1aa0c623 (direct backend), so the wasm backend is not the cause. It was not introduced by the no-fallback work (b1ead23).\n- 536870912 is HEAP_MAX_FLOOR, the lower bound of the heap cap (`heap_max_bytes`, std/src/gc.rs). The whole cap is reserved up front by one `alloc_zeroed`, which on wasm is a `memory.grow` of 8192 pages.\n- The linker declares the shared memory with a maximum of 16384 pages (1 GB, SHARED_MEMORY_MAX_PAGES in ash_wasm_link), so the module's own declaration allows it.\n- Ash's own host grants it: the Haxe `threads` conformance suite under wasm-fibers, run by `ash run`, passes with the same heap.\n- The other Caribou wasm tests, which are not threaded, pass.\n\nNot established: what refuses the grow under `caribou run`. Candidates are a memory limit or reservation the Caribou host sets on its wasmtime store, the machine (this was seen on a Mac with 16 GB under heavy load), or something specific to a threaded module run that way. Nothing was bisected.\n\nNext steps:\n1. Run the same built module with `ash run` instead of `caribou run`. If it runs, the difference is the host.\n2. Run it under `caribou run` with `ASH_GC_HEAP_MB=64` (a floor of 32 MB applies). If that passes, the module is fine and the host's memory grant is smaller than 512 MB.\n3. If it is the host, either the Caribou host raises its limit or the heap cap on wasm stops reserving the whole floor up front.\n\nReproducer: in a copy of caribou with the ash crates patched to a local checkout, `cargo test --release -p caribou-driver --features llvm --test linked futures_settle`.","files":null}]}